  "title": "Why Nobody Asks the Question in Meetings #shorts",
  "description": "Ever nodded while totally lost? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who nods at everything. Mae nods through Otto's meeting, lost, and sure she's the only one. In 'Pluralistic Ignorance and Alcohol Use on Campus: Some Consequences of Misperceiving the Social Norm' (Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 1993), Deborah Prentice and Dale Miller found Princeton students believed they were more uncomfortable with campus drinking than the average student. Everyone kept the same private doubt and assumed they were alone in it. Psychologists call it pluralistic ignorance. Ask the question. #psychology #shorts #pluralisticignorance #overthinking #work",
